{{Term/Store|''Misa's Recipe Book''||Series, BotW, TotK}},{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK}}<ref>{{Cite|Misa's Recipe Book|Game Screen|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Misa's Recipe Book|Game Screen|TotK}}</ref> also known as the '''''Book of Recipes''''',{{Exp Game|BotW}}<ref name="Book">{{Cite|We carry just about everything—from items for self-defense to everyday groceries. By all means, please peruse the {{Color BotW|Blue|book of recipes}} there, and buy some of our fine ingredients!|Misa|BotW}}</ref> is a recurring [[Object]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
''Misa's Recipe Book'' can be found at [[The Slippery Falcon]], located in [[Rito Village]]. It belongs to the shop's proprietor, [[Misa]], who encourages [[Link]] to read it.<ref name="Book"/> Within it, recipes for [[Apple Pie]], [[Nutcake]], and [[Fried Bananas]] are written.

====Transcription====
{{Tabs
|-
| Apple pie.
| {{Transcript|First, you'll want to buy {{Color BotW|Blue|Tabantha wheat}}, {{Color BotW|Blue|goat butter}}, and {{Color BotW|Blue|cane sugar}} here at the {{Color BotW|Blue|Slippery Falcon}}.<br/><br/>Cook those ingredients with an {{Color BotW|Blue|apple}} until the crust is a flaky golden brown and the insides are gooey and delicious.<br/><br/>And for an added kick, try substituting the apple with something else!}}
|-
| Nutcake.
| {{Transcript|First, you'll want to buy {{Color BotW|Blue|Tabantha wheat}}, {{Color BotW|Blue|goat butter}}, and {{Color BotW|Blue|cane sugar}} here at the {{Color BotW|Blue|Slippery Falcon}}.<br/><br/>Toss these ingredients in a pot alongside the nuts of your choice to make a tasty {{Color BotW|Blue|nutcake}}! I prefer {{Color BotW|Blue|acorns}} myself.}}
|-
| Fried bananas.
| {{Transcript|First, you'll want to buy {{Color BotW|Blue|Tabantha wheat}} and {{Color BotW|Blue|cane sugar}} here at the {{Color BotW|Blue|Slippery Falcon}}!<br/><br/>Then, just fry those up alongside some {{Color BotW|Blue|mighty bananas}}! {{Color BotW|Blue|Mighty bananas}} are rare in these parts, but this dish is worth it!}}
}}

==={{TotK|-}}===
''Misa's Recipe Book'' remains in [[The Slippery Falcon]]. Two new [[Recipe]]s have been added to its contents, though it has lost two others as a result. The Recipes that are detailed are [[Hot Buttered Apple]], [[Nutcake]], and [[Fish Pie]]. Prior to the completion of the "[[Tulin of Rito Village]]" [[Main Quest]], the Recipes for Nutcake and Fish Pie will be prefaced with a note that certain [[Ingredient]]s are in short supply due to the [[Blizzard]].<ref>{{Cite|Some ingredients may be in short supply due to the blizzard. We appreciate your patience as we restock.|Misa's Recipe Book|TotK}}</ref>

====Transcription====
{{Tabs
| Hot Buttered Apple
| {{Transcript|First, you'll want to buy {{Color TotK|Red|goat butter}} here at the Slippery Falcon.<br/><br/>Simply cook {{Color TotK|Red|goat butter}} and an {{Color TotK|Red|apple}} together, and the {{Color TotK|Red|hot buttered apple}} is complete!<br/><br/>Adding a {{Color TotK|Red|spicy pepper}} to the mix is a good way to warm up your whole body.}}
|-
| Nutcake
| {{Transcript|First, you'll want to buy {{Color TotK|Red|Tabantha wheat}}, {{Color TotK|Red|goat butter}}, and {{Color TotK|Red|cane sugar}} here at the Slippery Falcon.<br/><br/>Toss these three ingredients in a pot alongside your favorite type of {{Color TotK|Red|nut}} to make nutcake.<br/><br/>And for an added kick, try substituting the nut with something else!}}
|-
| Fish Pie
| {{Transcript|First, you'll want to buy {{Color TotK|Red|Tabantha wheat}} and {{Color TotK|Red|goat butter}} here at the Slippery Falcon.<br/><br/>Along with those, add {{Color TotK|Red|rock salt}} and your choice of {{Color TotK|Red|fish}} and cook them all together. Ta-da! A {{Color TotK|Red|fish pie}} ready to eat!<br/><br/>If you don't have {{Color TotK|Red|rock salt}}, you might find some by mining from ore deposits.}}
}}

